# More vectors written afresh from the FIX specification (FIX 4.4 / FIXT.1.1 message format,
# BodyLength and CheckSum rules, repeating group layout). The CATEGORIES of malformed input,
# checksum and repeating-group cases are inspired by the test inventories of QuickFIX/Go
# (parser_test.go, message_test.go, validation_test.go, repeating_group_test.go) and fix8
# (utests/message_test.cpp), and by quickfix test/definitions/server/fix44 file names.
# Nothing is copied: every message, field value, symbol, ID and timestamp here is new.
# Expected outcomes follow include/glaze/fix/scan.hpp (parse_fields / validate / frame / checksum).

id = spec.cks_plus_one
source = spec
kind = validate
msg = 8=FIX.4.4|9=54|35=0|49=NODEA|56=NODEB|34=17|52=20261105-08:15:30.250|10=213|
expect = error
note = category from quickfixgo validation_test: CheckSum one above the true sum

id = spec.cks_minus_one
source = spec
kind = validate
msg = 8=FIX.4.4|9=54|35=0|49=NODEA|56=NODEB|34=17|52=20261105-08:15:30.250|10=211|
expect = error
note = category from quickfixgo validation_test: CheckSum one below the true sum

id = spec.cks_above_255
source = spec
kind = validate
msg = 8=FIX.4.4|9=54|35=0|49=NODEA|56=NODEB|34=17|52=20261105-08:15:30.250|10=999|
expect = error
note = category from quickfixgo validation_test: CheckSum value 256..999 can never match

id = spec.cks_zero_mismatch
source = spec
kind = validate
msg = 8=FIX.4.4|9=54|35=0|49=NODEA|56=NODEB|34=17|52=20261105-08:15:30.250|10=000|
expect = error
note = category from quickfixgo validation_test: CheckSum 000 when the sum is not zero

